hey this is fresh tall Walker a single  alien lands on earth every day after  that each alien on earth undergoes a  transformation which could be any of the  four equally likely events the alien  could die the alien could do nothing the  alien could replicate itself which means  there are two aliens in total or the  alien could replicate itself two times  which means there are three aliens total  what is the probability the alien race  eventually dies out and goes extinct  this question is sometimes asked as an  interview question for technical jobs  can you figure it out give this problem  a try and when you're ready keep  watching the video for the solution  let's write P for the probability that  an alien and all of its descendants die  out the probability that one alien and  all of its descendants die out is P the  next day there are four equally likely  events there is a 25% chance that this  alien could die out this means there's a  conditional probability of one that this  alien and all of its descendants die out  there is another contingency or the  alien does nothing now the situation is  exactly the same this means the  probability is still P that this alien  and all of its descendants will die out  there's also a 25% chance the alien will  replicate itself so that there are two  aliens now each of these aliens will  have a probability P that this alien and  all of its descendants will die out each  of these lines of aliens will be  independent from each other the  probability that both of them  and all of their descendants I out will  be the product P times P equals P  squared in the final 25% case the alien  replicates itself two times each of  these aliens has a probability P of  dying out and having all of their  descendants die out each of these  branches is independent from each other  the probability that all three die out  will be equal to P times P times P which  is P cubed if the probability is to  exist it must satisfy the following  equation the probability of an alien and  all of its descendants dying out has to  be equal to 0.25 times the quantity 1  plus P plus P squared plus P cubed in  the theory of statistical branching  processes the probability of extinction  is equal to the smallest positive root  of this equation this is equal to the  square root of 2 minus 1 which is  approximately 41.4% and that's the  answer now to be comprehensive we should  consider the other solutions to this  equation one solution is negative and  that can be disregarded because a  probability cannot be negative but the  other solution is equal to 1 this would  mean there's a probability of 1 that  it's surely going to happen that the  aliens would go extinct how do we know  that this is not the solution and that  the correct solution is 41.4% to figure  that out we have to dig deeper into the  details and consider the discrete  version of the problem let's write P sub  K for the probability of an alien and  all of its descendants dying out in K  days let's consider the probability that  an alien dies out in k plus 1 days there  are four things that can happen the next  day there's a 25% chance the alien dies  out  in which case the conditional  probability of dying out in K plus-1  days is equal to one there's a 25%  chance the alien does nothing now one  day has already passed so in order for  this alien and all of its descendants to  die out in K plus-1 days the next day  this alien and all of its descendants  would have to die out in K days it would  have to be one day less the conditional  probability here is P sub K in the 25%  chance the alien replicates itself so  there are two aliens each of these  aliens and all of their descendants  would have to die out in K days this is  a conditional probability of P sub K  squared in the final case the alien  replicates itself two times and each of  these aliens and have a P sub K chance  that that alien and all of its  descendants would die out in K days the  probability of all of them dying out  would be the product which is P sub K  cubed now one thing to notice here is  that the expected number of aliens the  next day is equal to zero plus one plus  two plus three all divided by four this  is equal to 1.5 which is greater than  one that means the alien is more than  replicating itself on average so we can  expect that there's a chance the aliens  would survive the probability of  extinction should not be equal to one it  should be less than one  so how do we know this is true we have  this recursive equation for the  probability the alien dies out in k plus  one days in terms of the probability  that it would die out in K days we're  going to show that this probability is  always less than or equal to the square  root of two minus one now what's the  probability an alien would die out in  exactly one day well that's only the 25%  chance that it simply dies out in the  following day this is our base case now  we assume this is true for all values  less than or equal less than P sub K  plus  one so we have this recurrence relation  and we can now apply the induction  hypothesis on all the terms piece of  clay so we'll substitute in square root  of 2 minus 1 for those terms and this  all simplifies to be square root of 2  minus 1 so we have an increasing  sequence of P sub K because the  probability keeps increasing as we  expand the number of days this is an  increasing sequence and we know it's  bounded by square root of 2 minus 1 so  in fact this sequence will converge to  the value of square root of 2 minus 1  and that in fact is the correct answer  to this problem did you figure it out  thanks for watching this video please  subscribe to my channel I make videos on  math and game theory you can catch me on  my blog mind your decisions which you  can follow on Facebook Google+ and  patreon you can catch me on social media  at pressure soccer and if you like this  video please check out my books there  links in the video descripti